                <invention-title lang="de">ELEKTROCHIRURGISCHER STIFT</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">CRAYON ÉLECTROCHIRURGICAL</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">AN ELECTROSURGICAL PENCIL</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An electro-surgical pencil 1 is provided. The pencil comprises a housing 2 forming an axially extending main suction passage from a proximal opening to a distal opening. The housing comprises (i) a main body 11 forming the axially extending main suction passage and the distal opening, and (ii) a switch 6, 7 on the main body. The pencil further comprises a tube 3 with an internal conduit extending between a distal extension opening and a proximal extension opening and forming an extension of the axially extending main suction passage to the proximal extension opening, the tube being configured for telescoping movement through the proximal opening of the housing. The pencil still further comprises an electrode 5 for cutting and/or coagulating tissue, the electrode being attached to the tube and extending axially from the proximal extension opening, wherein the switch is configured to provide a signal to cause an electrosurgical radiofrequency, RF, signal to be supplied to the electrode, and a suction tip 9 attached to the tube and forming a further extension of the axially extending main suction passage. While the electrode remains in a fixed position relative to the tube, the suction tip is configured for telescoping movement relative to the tube to adjust an extent by which the suction tip covers a portion of the electrode, wherein the suction tip is receivable in a recess in the housing, wherein the suction tip is slidable along the tube to a distal position at which a portion of the suction tip is slid below the switch.</p>
            </abstract>
